              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            the Galois group of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extension"} field extension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L/K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            naturally associated to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %p
            Galois cohomology is studied notably in the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number+theory"} algebraic number theory
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_tale_cohomology Relation to étale cohomology
          %p
            Galois cohomology of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is essentially the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+cohomology"} étale cohomology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(k)
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison+theorem+%28%C3%A9tale+cohomology%29"} comparison theorem (étale cohomology)
          %h3#InCohesiveHomotopyTypeTheory In terms of cohesive homotopy type theory
          %p
            We make some comments on the formulation of Galois cohomology in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
          %p
            As discussed at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+theory"} Galois theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+Galois+group"} absolute Galois group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi Galois
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{Galois}
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \coloneqq Spec(K)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi Galois
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{Galois}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi Galois
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi_1(X)  \simeq \mathbf{B}G_{Galois}
                  \\,.
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            there exists the
            = succeed "-construction" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            –
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \colon Type \;\vdash \; \Pi(X) \colon Type
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, by the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            in the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/group%20cohomology#InHomotopyTypeTheory"} group cohomology - In terms of homotopy type theory
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi Galois
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{Galois}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi Galois
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{Galois}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
                over the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function type
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mi Galois
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mo *
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Type
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\vdash \; \left( \prod_{x \colon \mathbf{B}G_{Galois}} \left( * \to A \right)\right) \colon Type
                      \\,.
          %p
            Hence, generally in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x \colon \Pi(X) \;\vdash \; A(x) \colon Type
          %p
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-Galois cohomology
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo )
                    %mo )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash \; \left( \prod_{x \colon \Pi(X)} \left( * \to A\right) \right)
                  \\colon Type
                  \\,.
          %p
            %strong Warning.
            Currently there is not written down yet a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type+theory"} cohesive homotopy type theory
            given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            like the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert%27s+theorem+90"} Hilbert's theorem 90
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number+theory"} algebraic number theory
          %h2#literature Literature
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Tate"}> John Tate
                ,
                %em Galois cohomology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://modular.math.washington.edu/edu/2010/582e/refs/tate-galois_cohomology.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Pierre+Serre"}> Jean-Pierre Serre
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Galois cohomology
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-59141-9"} 10.1007/978-3-642-59141-9
              %p
                %em> Cohomologie galoisienne
                , Lecture Notes in Mathematics, 5 (Fifth ed. 1994), Springer-Verlag, MR1324577 doi:
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0108758"} 10.1007/BFb0108758)
            %li#GilleSzamuely06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philippe+Gille"}> Philippe Gille
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tam%C3%A1s+Szamuely"} Tamás Szamuely
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Central Simple Algebras and Galois Cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511607219"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511607219
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ens.fr/~benoist/refs/Gille-Szamuely.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Grégory Berhuy,
                %em An introduction to Galois cohomology and its applications
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www-fourier.ujf-grenoble.fr/~berhuy/fichiers/NTUcourse.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                M. Kneser,
                %em Lectures on Galois cohomology of classical groups
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.tifr.res.in/~publ/ln/tifr47.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galois_cohomology"} Galois cohomology
          %p
            A generalization in the setup of
            = succeed "s:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coring"} coring
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomasz+Brzezi%C5%84ski"}> Tomasz Brzeziński
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Descent cohomology and corings
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0601491"} math.RA/0601491
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theoretic
            context:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anand+Pillay"}> Anand Pillay
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Remarks on Galois cohomology and definability
              = succeed ":2" do
                %strong 62
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2275542"} doi
            %li
              B. Poizat,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Une theorie de Galois imaginaire
              %strong 48
              (1983) 1151-1170.
